an> a.<span class=\"me1\">id</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw1\">public</span><span class=\"sy4\">:</span>\n        A<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">int</span> i<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy4\">:</span> id <span class=\"br0\">{</span>i<span class=\"br0\">}</span> <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n        A<span class=\"br0\">(</span>A <span class=\"kw4\">const</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> delete<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        A<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> operator <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>A <span class=\"kw4\">const</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> delete<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">int</span> a <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu0\">5</span>, b <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu0\">3</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1774\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> a <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">' '</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> b <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">swap</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>a, b<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1774\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> a <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">' '</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> b <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    Ns<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">A</span> p <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"nu0\">6</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span>, q <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"nu0\">9</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1774\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> p <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">' '</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> q <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"co1\">//  std::swap(p, q); // error, type requirements are not satisfied</span>\n    swap<span class=\"br0\">(</span>p, q<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>      <span class=\"co1\">// OK, ADL finds the appropriate friend `swap`</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1774\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> p <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">' '</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> q <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>5 3\n3 5\nA::id=6 A::id=9\nswap(A::id=6, A::id=9)\nA::id=9 A::id=6</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"Defect_reports\">Defect reports</h3>\n<p>The following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards.\n</p>\n<table class=\"dsctable\">\n<tr>\n<th>DR\n</th>\n<th>Applied to\n</th>\n<th>Behavior as published\n</th>\n<th>Correct behavior\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue227\" data-external=\"1\">LWG 227</a>\n</td>\n<td>C++98\n</td>\n<td><code>T</code> was not required to be <a href=\"/w/cpp/named_req/CopyConstructible\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">CopyConstructible</em></a> or <a href=\"/w/cpp/named_req/DefaultConstructible\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">DefaultConstructible</em></a><br>(a temporary object of type <code>T</code> might not be able to be constructed)\n</td>\n<td><code>T</code> is also required to<br>be <a href=\"/w/cpp/named_req/CopyConstructible\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">CopyConstructible</em></a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue809\" data-external=\"1\">LWG 809</a>\n</td>\n<td>C++98\n</td>\n<td>arrays could not be swapped\n</td>\n<td>added overload <span class=\"t-v\">(2)</span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue2554\" data-external=\"1\">LWG 2554</a>\n</td>\n<td>C++11\n</td>\n<td>swapping multi-dimensional arrays can never<br>be <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span></span> due to name lookup problems\n</td>\n<td>made to work\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/ranges/swap\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>ranges::swap</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td> swaps the values of two objects<br><span class=\"t-mark\">(customization point object)</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/algorithm/iter_swap\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>iter_swap</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  swaps the elements pointed to by two iterators <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/algorithm/swap_ranges\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>swap_ranges</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  swaps two ranges of elements <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/exchange\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>exchange</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx14\">(C++14)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  replaces the argument with a new value and returns its previous value <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Exceptions","id":"Exceptions"},{"depth":3,"text":"Complexity","id":"Complexity"},{"depth":3,"text":"Specializations","id":"Specializations"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"Defect reports","id":"Defect_reports"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"algorithm","title":"Algorithms library"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::swap","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations. Exchanges the given values."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"a, b"},{"label":"Return value","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Exceptions","note":"(none) (until C++11) noexcept specification: noexcept( std::is_nothrow_move_constructible<T>::value && std::is_nothrow_move_assignable<T>::value ) (since C++11)"},{"label":"Complexity","note":"Constant."},{"label":"Specializations","note":"The expected way to make a program-defined type swappable is to provide a non-member function swap in the same namespace as the type: see Swappable for details.","children":[{"label":"std::swap(std::pair)","note":"specializes the std::swap algorithm"},{"label":"std: